.nh
.TH "PB-POLICY-GET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-policy-get - Print the saved workspace policy


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb policy get [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the saved policy file of the active workspace exactly as it was saved,
comments included, so it can be edited and saved again with pb policy set.
Use --version to print an earlier version; pb policy versions lists them. With
--json, print the whole policy record: version, digest, author and the names
the policy may use.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for get

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--version\fP=0
	print this saved version instead of the current one


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb policy get > policy.hujson
  pb policy get --version 3
  pb policy get --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-policy(1)\fP
